Greek tiny-voca checkpoint and inference adapter

The released Greek model weights and sample WAVs are CC BY 4.0. The inference
adapter source code in src/tiny_voca_gr/ is Apache-2.0. See LICENSE and
LICENSE-CODE, respectively.

The model architecture and upstream implementation are based on tiny-voca by
Muhammed Nazeem: https://github.com/n4ze3m/tiny-voca (Apache-2.0). The Greek
checkpoint was trained from scratch and does not contain the upstream English
checkpoint.

Training recordings and author-created annotations came from STOMA by Michail
Raptakis, Yannis Pantazis, and Alexandros Angelakis:
https://huggingface.co/datasets/aangelakis/STOMA (CC BY 4.0).
The dataset maintainers requested citation of their work and advised that their
paper has been submitted to Language Resources and Evaluation (Springer) and is
under revision. The dataset and its transcripts are not distributed here.

The STOMA dataset license does not cover third-party textual material, including
the CGL Text Bank. Such material retains the terms of its original source.

eSpeak NG is a separate GPL-3.0-or-later program used by the Greek phoneme
frontend. It is not bundled in this repository.
